{#
The answer to a bulk action: redraw the list, once.

Not a stream per row, which is what the toolbar's per-conversation posts
produced. Each of those knew what had happened to its own row and nothing else,
so a list that lost four of five rows still said "1–5 of 5", and one that lost
every row showed no empty state at all — the pager and the placeholder are
properties of the LIST, and no row-shaped response can carry them.

So this body carries no streams at all: the CLIENT reloads the list frame when
the request comes back, and the controller answers that reload exactly as it
answers any other visit to the list. One definition of what the list looks like,
and no second implementation here of the paging, filtering and sorting this
response has no parameters for.

A `<turbo-stream action="refresh">` was tried first and is not reliable enough
for this: it asks Turbo to refresh the PAGE, which is debounced and skipped
under conditions this code cannot see. Rows that leave the list happened to look
right — they were gone either way — while rows that STAY, like a conversation
being marked read, kept their old state on screen until something else
re-rendered them.

The count is a comment rather than anything visible. Nothing on screen needs it,
and a bulk action that silently does nothing is otherwise indistinguishable from
one that worked — which is exactly how a whole-view archive that resynced only
the first thread's labels answered 200, reported 71, and changed nothing.

## Why the rows are here as well as the frame reload

The rows are redrawn from here AND the client re-reads the list frame, which
looks like doing the same work twice and is not. The rows have to change the
moment the response lands, because that is the feedback for the click; the frame
has to be re-read because the pager and the empty state are properties of the
list that no row-shaped stream can carry. Leaving out the first made a bulk
mark-read take a visible beat and left the rows stale in between; leaving out
the second is the original finding.

Variables:
  count    how many conversations were acted on; 0 is a valid answer
  threads  the conversations, for redrawing their rows
  leaves   true when the action takes them out of THIS list (archive, trash,
           restore) rather than changing them in place (read)
#}
<!-- plmail-bulk: {{ count }} -->

{% for thread in threads %}
    {% if leaves %}
        <turbo-stream action="remove" target="thread_{{ thread.id }}">
        </turbo-stream>
    {% else %}
        <turbo-stream action="replace" target="thread_{{ thread.id }}">
            <template>
                {% include '_partials/_thread_row.html.twig' with { thread: thread } only %}
            </template>
        </turbo-stream>
    {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
